  },

  expected_trace: String.raw`THINK OBSERVE.
SAW alignment(front=wR@c1,middle=wB@c2,back=bR@c8)
SAW checks_by_middle=[Bh7+]

CANDIDATES Bh7+[alignment,check]
TRY 22.Bh7+ BECAUSE:
  alignment(wR@c1,wB@c2,bR@c8)
  check(Bh7+)

THINK OPPONENT.
SAW legal_replies=[Kxh7,Kh8] count=2

RULE enumerate_all_if_legal_replies_at_most_2
ORDER Kxh7 first because capture(Kxh7,wB@h7)
REPLIES [Kxh7[capture],Kh8[king_move]]

LINE 1.

REPLY 22...Kxh7 BECAUSE capture(Kxh7,wB@h7)

THINK OBSERVE.
SAW alignment_square_cleared(c2)
SAW captures_of_back=[Rxc8]

CANDIDATES Rxc8[capture_back_of_alignment]
TRY 23.Rxc8 BECAUSE:
  alignment(front=wR@c1,back=bR@c8)
  capture(Rxc8,bR@c8)

THINK OPPONENT.
SAW legal_reply_count>2

RULE use_reply_classes_if_more_than_2_legal_replies
CLASS recapture -> [Rxc8]

REPORT If Black does not recapture, the rook captured on c8 stays won.

REPLY 23...Rxc8 BECAUSE recapture(Rxc8,c8)

THINK OBSERVE.
SAW recaptures=[Qxc8]

CANDIDATES Qxc8[recapture]
TRY 24.Qxc8 BECAUSE recapture(Qxc8,c8)

WE WIN: White gets both black rooks for one rook and one bishop.
REPORT branch=Kxh7 result=gain_at_least_exchange

BACKTRACK TO 22.Bh7+.

LINE 2.

REPLY 22...Kh8 BECAUSE king_move(Kh8)

THINK OBSERVE.
SAW alignment_square_cleared(c2)
SAW captures_of_back=[Rxc8]

CANDIDATES Rxc8[capture_back_of_alignment]
TRY 23.Rxc8 BECAUSE:
  alignment(front=wR@c1,back=bR@c8)
  capture(Rxc8,bR@c8)

THINK OPPONENT.
SAW legal_reply_count>2

RULE use_reply_classes_if_more_than_2_legal_replies
CLASS recapture -> [Rxc8]

REPORT If Black does not recapture, the rook captured on c8 stays won.

REPLY 23...Rxc8 BECAUSE recapture(Rxc8,c8)

THINK OBSERVE.
SAW recaptures=[Qxc8+]

CANDIDATES Qxc8+[recapture]
TRY 24.Qxc8+ BECAUSE recapture(Qxc8+,c8)

WE WIN: White gets both black rooks for one rook and keeps the bishop.
REPORT branch=Kh8 result=gain_greater_than_exchange

END SOLVE every_legal_reply_to_Bh7+_wins_at_least_the_exchange`,

  expected_pgn: String.raw`[Event "Woodpecker 44 — Move the Middle Piece with Check"]
[Site "https://lichess.org/analysis/standard/2r2rk1/pQ1n1pp1/1p2p2p/3p4/P2P4/4P2P/1qB2PP1/2R2RK1_w_-_-_0_22"]
[SetUp "1"]
[FEN "2r2rk1/pQ1n1pp1/1p2p2p/3p4/P2P4/4P2P/1qB2PP1/2R2RK1 w - - 0 22"]
[Result "*"]
[Policy "move-middle-with-check/v1"]
[Goal "gain at least the exchange"]

22. Bh7+!
    {The rook on c1, bishop on c2, and black rook on c8
     form an alignment.

     The bishop is the middle piece. Bh7+ moves the middle
     piece out of the line with check.

     Black has only two legal replies, so both are enumerated.
     Kxh7 is examined first because it captures the bishop.}

22... Kxh7
    {The materially strongest reply: capture the checking bishop.}

    (22... Kh8
        {The only other legal reply. The king does not take
         the bishop.}

        23. Rxc8
            {With c2 clear, the front piece captures the back
             piece of the alignment.}

        23... Rxc8
            {The remaining rook recaptures. If Black does not
             recapture, White has already won the c8 rook.}

        24. Qxc8+
            {White recaptures and has won both black rooks for
             one white rook while keeping the bishop.})

23. Rxc8
    {With c2 clear, the front piece captures the back piece
     of the alignment.}

23... Rxc8
    {The remaining rook recaptures. If Black does not
     recapture, White has already won the c8 rook.}

24. Qxc8
    {White recaptures. Even after Black chose the materially
     strongest king reply, White obtained both black rooks
     for one rook and one bishop.}
*`
};
